#: ../../../scsi/ufs.rst:5
msgid "Universal Flash Storage"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../scsi/ufs.rst:26
msgid "1. Overview"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../scsi/ufs.rst:28
msgid ""
"Universal Flash Storage (UFS) is a storage specification for flash devices. "
"It aims to provide a universal storage interface for both embedded and "
"removable flash memory-based storage in mobile devices such as smart phones "
"and tablet computers. The specification is defined by JEDEC Solid State "
"Technology Association. UFS is based on the MIPI M-PHY physical layer "
"standard. UFS uses MIPI M-PHY as the physical layer and MIPI Unipro as the "
"link layer."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../scsi/ufs.rst:36
msgid "The main goals of UFS are to provide:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../scsi/ufs.rst:38
msgid "Optimized performance:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../scsi/ufs.rst:40
msgid "For UFS version 1.0 and 1.1 the target performance is as follows:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../scsi/ufs.rst:42
msgid "Support for Gear1 is mandatory (rate A: 1248Mbps, rate B: 1457.6Mbps)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../scsi/ufs.rst:43
msgid "Support for Gear2 is optional (rate A: 2496Mbps, rate B: 2915.2Mbps)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../scsi/ufs.rst:45
msgid "Future version of the standard,"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../scsi/ufs.rst:47
msgid "Gear3 (rate A: 4992Mbps, rate B: 5830.4Mbps)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../scsi/ufs.rst:49
msgid "Low power consumption"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../scsi/ufs.rst:50
msgid "High random IOPs and low latency"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../scsi/ufs.rst:54
msgid "2. UFS Architecture Overview"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../scsi/ufs.rst:56
msgid ""
"UFS has a layered communication architecture which is based on SCSI SAM-5 "
"architectural model."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../scsi/ufs.rst:59
msgid "UFS communication architecture consists of the following layers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../scsi/ufs.rst:62
msgid "2.1 Application Layer"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../scsi/ufs.rst:64
msgid ""
"The Application layer is composed of the UFS command set layer (UCS), Task "
"Manager and Device manager. The UFS interface is designed to be protocol "
"agnostic, however SCSI has been selected as a baseline protocol for versions "
"1.0 and 1.1 of the UFS protocol layer."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../scsi/ufs.rst:69
msgid "UFS supports a subset of SCSI commands defined by SPC-4 and SBC-3."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../scsi/ufs.rst:71
msgid "UCS:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../scsi/ufs.rst:72
msgid "It handles SCSI commands supported by UFS specification."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../scsi/ufs.rst:73
msgid "Task manager:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../scsi/ufs.rst:74
msgid ""
"It handles task management functions defined by the UFS which are meant for "
"command queue control."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../scsi/ufs.rst:76
msgid "Device manager:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../scsi/ufs.rst:77
msgid ""
"It handles device level operations and device configuration operations. "
"Device level operations mainly involve device power management operations "
"and commands to Interconnect layers. Device level configurations involve "
"handling of query requests which are used to modify and retrieve "
"configuration information of the device."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../scsi/ufs.rst:85
msgid "2.2 UFS Transport Protocol (UTP) layer"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../scsi/ufs.rst:87
msgid ""
"The UTP layer provides services for the higher layers through Service Access "
"Points. UTP defines 3 service access points for higher layers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../scsi/ufs.rst:91
msgid ""
"UDM_SAP: Device manager service access point is exposed to device manager "
"for device level operations. These device level operations are done through "
"query requests."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../scsi/ufs.rst:94
msgid ""
"UTP_CMD_SAP: Command service access point is exposed to UFS command set "
"layer (UCS) to transport commands."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../scsi/ufs.rst:96
msgid ""
"UTP_TM_SAP: Task management service access point is exposed to task manager "
"to transport task management functions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../scsi/ufs.rst:99
msgid "UTP transports messages through UFS protocol information unit (UPIU)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../scsi/ufs.rst:102
msgid "2.3 UFS Interconnect (UIC) Layer"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../scsi/ufs.rst:104
msgid ""
"UIC is the lowest layer of the UFS layered architecture. It handles the "
"connection between UFS host and UFS device. UIC consists of MIPI UniPro and "
"MIPI M-PHY. UIC provides 2 service access points to upper layer:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../scsi/ufs.rst:109
msgid "UIC_SAP: To transport UPIU between UFS host and UFS device."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../scsi/ufs.rst:110
msgid "UIO_SAP: To issue commands to Unipro layers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../scsi/ufs.rst:114
msgid "3. UFSHCD Overview"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../scsi/ufs.rst:116
msgid ""
"The UFS host controller driver is based on the Linux SCSI Framework. UFSHCD "
"is a low-level device driver which acts as an interface between the SCSI "
"Midlayer and PCIe-based UFS host controllers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../scsi/ufs.rst:120
msgid "The current UFSHCD implementation supports the following functionality:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../scsi/ufs.rst:123
msgid "3.1 UFS controller initialization"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../scsi/ufs.rst:125
msgid ""
"The initialization module brings the UFS host controller to active state and "
"prepares the controller to transfer commands/responses between UFSHCD and "
"UFS device."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../scsi/ufs.rst:130
msgid "3.2 UTP Transfer requests"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../scsi/ufs.rst:132
msgid ""
"Transfer request handling module of UFSHCD receives SCSI commands from the "
"SCSI Midlayer, forms UPIUs and issues the UPIUs to the UFS Host controller. "
"Also, the module decodes responses received from the UFS host controller in "
"the form of UPIUs and intimates the SCSI Midlayer of the status of the "
"command."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../scsi/ufs.rst:139
msgid "3.3 UFS error handling"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../scsi/ufs.rst:141
msgid ""
"Error handling module handles Host controller fatal errors, Device fatal "
"errors and UIC interconnect layer-related errors."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../scsi/ufs.rst:145
msgid "3.4 SCSI Error handling"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../scsi/ufs.rst:147
msgid ""
"This is done through UFSHCD SCSI error handling routines registered with the "
"SCSI Midlayer. Examples of some of the error handling commands issues by the "
"SCSI Midlayer are Abort task, LUN reset and host reset. UFSHCD Routines to "
"perform these tasks are registered with SCSI Midlayer "
"through .eh_abort_handler, .eh_device_reset_handler "
"and .eh_host_reset_handler."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../scsi/ufs.rst:154
msgid ""
"In this version of UFSHCD, Query requests and power management functionality "
"are not implemented."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../scsi/ufs.rst:158
msgid "4. BSG Support"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../scsi/ufs.rst:160
msgid ""
"This transport driver supports exchanging UFS protocol information units "
"(UPIUs) with a UFS device. Typically, user space will allocate struct "
"ufs_bsg_request and struct ufs_bsg_reply (see ufs_bsg.h) as request_upiu and "
"reply_upiu respectively.  Filling those UPIUs should be done in accordance "
"with JEDEC spec UFS2.1 paragraph 10.7. *Caveat emptor*: The driver makes no "
"further input validations and sends the UPIU to the device as it is.  Open "
"the bsg device in /dev/ufs-bsg and send SG_IO with the applicable sg_io_v4::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../scsi/ufs.rst:184
msgid ""
"If you wish to read or write a descriptor, use the appropriate xferp of "
"sg_io_v4."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../scsi/ufs.rst:187
msgid ""
"The userspace tool that interacts with the ufs-bsg endpoint and uses its "
"UPIU-based protocol is available at:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../scsi/ufs.rst:190
msgid "https://github.com/westerndigitalcorporation/ufs-tool"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../scsi/ufs.rst:192
msgid ""
"For more detailed information about the tool and its supported features, "
"please see the tool's README."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../scsi/ufs.rst:195
msgid "UFS specifications can be found at:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../scsi/ufs.rst:197
msgid "UFS - http://www.jedec.org/sites/default/files/docs/JESD220.pdf"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../scsi/ufs.rst:198
msgid "UFSHCI - http://www.jedec.org/sites/default/files/docs/JESD223.pdf"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../scsi/ufs.rst:201
msgid "5. UFS Reference Clock Frequency configuration"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../scsi/ufs.rst:203
msgid ""
"Devicetree can define a clock named \"ref_clk\" under the UFS controller "
"node to specify the intended reference clock frequency for the UFS storage "
"parts. ACPI-based system can specify the frequency using ACPI Device-"
"Specific Data property named \"ref-clk-freq\". In both ways the value is "
"interpreted as frequency in Hz and must match one of the values given in the "
"UFS specification. UFS subsystem will attempt to read the value when "
"executing common controller initialization. If the value is available, UFS "
"subsystem will ensure the bRefClkFreq attribute of the UFS storage device is "
"set accordingly and will modify it if there is a mismatch."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../scsi/ufs.rst:214
msgid "6. Testing with QEMU"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../scsi/ufs.rst:216
msgid ""
"QEMU emulates a UFS host controller as a PCI device named \"ufs\" and "
"logical units named \"ufs-lu\". This can be used to test changes to the UFS "
"core and to ufshcd-pci without UFS hardware."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../scsi/ufs.rst:220
msgid ""
"The \"ufs\" and \"ufs-lu\" devices are available since QEMU 8.2, and the "
"\"mcq\" property since QEMU 9.1."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../scsi/ufs.rst:223
msgid ""
"Enable the following kernel options on top of the architecture defconfig::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../scsi/ufs.rst:230
msgid "Example for an arm64 guest with one 1 GiB logical unit::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../scsi/ufs.rst:240
msgid ""
"The logical unit appears as a SCSI disk (for example /dev/sda). Drop "
"\"mcq=on\" to test the single doorbell mode instead of MCQ. The same -device "
"options work with qemu-system-x86_64."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../scsi/ufs.rst:244
msgid ""
"The emulation accepts the link startup and hibernate enter/exit UIC commands "
"and, since QEMU 11.1, DME get/set and the power mode change sequence, but it "
"does not model UniPro, M-PHY or the resulting link state. Clock gating "
"hardware and vendor host drivers are not exercised either. Changes in those "
"areas still need testing on real hardware."
msgstr ""
